  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Speeding the adjustment of photosynthesis to shade-sun transitions to increase yield potential in the field</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Challenges Research Fund (GCRF) supports cutting-edge research to address challenges faced by developing countries. The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world. The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching goal of the International Wheat Yield Programme is to increase wheat grain yields by 50% in the next 20 years by targeting increases in genetic potential, leading to increased food security in DAC-listed countries. This project focusses on photosynthesis, working with Mexico, Iran, Pakistan, India and Tunisia.</narrative>
  </description>
